Cortex database migrations (Alembic, async engine via psycopg 3).

Commands (from the repository root):
    scripts\dev.cmd migrate                 upgrade to the latest revision
    scripts\dev.cmd migrate <revision>      upgrade/downgrade to a revision (e.g. -1, base)
    scripts\dev.cmd revision "message"      autogenerate a new revision from model changes

Rules:
  * Review every autogenerated migration by hand before committing.
  * Every migration needs a working downgrade(); tests/integration/test_migrations.py walks
    every revision up, down and up again, and fails if models and migrations drift apart.
  * Data migrations go in their own revision, separate from schema changes.
